  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l05_policy_value_training_step(features: list, pi_targets: list, z_targets: list, w_pi: list, b_pi: list, w_v: list, b_v: list, lr: float = 0.01) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Execute a single gradient descent parameter update on linear policy and value heads given mini-batch representations, search-policy targets, and empirical game outcomes.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nExecute a single gradient descent parameter update on linear policy and value heads given mini-batch representations, search-policy targets, and empirical game outcomes.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l05_policy_value_training_step(features: list, pi_targets: list, z_targets: list, w_pi: list, b_pi: list, w_v: list, b_v: list, lr: float = 0.01) -> dict:\n    X = np.array(features, dtype=float)\n    pi_t, z_t = np.array(pi_targets, dtype=float), np.array(z_targets, dtype=float)\n    W_pi, B_pi = np.array(w_pi, dtype=float), np.array(b_pi, dtype=float)\n    W_v, B_v = np.array(w_v, dtype=float), np.array(b_v, dtype=float)\n    logits = np.dot(X, W_pi) + B_pi\n    exp_l = np.exp(logits - np.max(logits, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    probs = exp_l / np.sum(exp_l, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    d_logits = (probs - pi_t) / len(X)\n    v_pred = np.tanh(np.dot(X, W_v) + B_v)\n    d_v = 2.0 * (v_pred - z_t) * (1.0 - v_pred ** 2) / len(X)\n    return {\n        'w_pi': np.round(W_pi - lr * np.dot(X.T, d_logits), 6).tolist(),\n        'b_pi': np.round(B_pi - lr * np.sum(d_logits, axis=0), 6).tolist(),\n        'w_v': np.round(W_v - lr * np.dot(X.T, d_v), 6).tolist(),\n        'b_v': np.round(B_v - lr * np.sum(d_v, axis=0), 6).tolist()\n    }\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
